WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:31.160
On November 26, 1922, egyptologist Howard
Carter entered the tomb he discovered just

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.540
a few weeks prior.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.970
After decades of fruitless searching, he found
something more amazing than he could have

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.230
ever hoped for.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:44.220
When asked if he saw anything inside, he simply
replied “Yes, wonderful things.”

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:49.750
Carter had located the tomb of a pharaoh from
the 18th dynasty who ruled over ancient Egypt

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:52.290
during the 14th century BC.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:57.940
More importantly, though, it was a tomb that
had been mostly undisturbed for over 3,000

00:00:57.940 --> 00:00:58.940
years.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:03.440
That pharaoh was Tutankhamun, who ascended
to the throne as a young boy and who died

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:05.000
when he reached adulthood.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.500
His life was short and lacked accomplishments,
but that did not matter.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:13.340
For Tutankhamun, death was only the beginning…

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:17.580
He achieved far more fame and glory in death
than he could have ever dreamed of while he

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.530
ruled over the land of the Nile.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:24.860
This young king and his tomb rich with artifacts
helped modern society understand ancient Egypt

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:30.980
far better than anyone else and, in the process,
turned King Tut into the most famous pharaoh

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:32.650
in history.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:35.800
Family Life

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:40.330
Ok, let’s start off with the name.

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:44.510
We all know him as Tutankhamun, but things
were not really that simple.

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:48.891
In fact, according to the royal protocol of
ancient Egypt, the full titulary of the pharaohs

00:01:48.891 --> 00:01:50.810
contained five names.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:54.710
First was their Horus name, the oldest cognomen
which dated all the way back to prehistory.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:58.130
In Tut’s case, this was Ka nakht tut mesut.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:03.870
Then came the Nebty name, or the Two Ladies,
referring to the goddesses Nekhbet and Wadjet.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:08.140
For Tut, this was Nefer hepu segereh tawy.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:13.739
Then there was the Golden Horus name which,
for Tut, was Wetjes khau sehotep netjeru.

00:02:13.739 --> 00:02:16.610
Lastly, there were the throne name, or prenomen,
and personal name, or nomen.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:21.230
They were the ones that pharaohs were typically
referred by and are similar to our standard

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:22.770
of first name and last name.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:26.640
For our young pharaoh, these were Neb kheperu
Ra and Tut ankh Amun.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.950
These last two names were always marked distinctly
in Egyptian inscriptions to show that they

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:36.200
referred to a royal name by encasing them
in an oval with a line at one end called a

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.200
cartouche.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.879
So, if we put it all together and translate
it, Tut’s full name would have been “The

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:44.969
strong bull, pleasing of birth; One of perfect
laws, who pacifies the Two Lands; Elevated

00:02:44.969 --> 00:02:51.159
of appearances who satisfied the gods; Lord
of the forms of Ra; The living image of Amun.”

00:02:51.159 --> 00:02:56.430
That’s quite the mouthful so it is not surprising
that most people simply call him Tutankhamun,

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:01.920
although there are some ancient inscriptions
with variants on his name which are even longer.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:06.560
You would think that is the end of it, but
there is actually one more point to make about

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:07.560
his name.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:13.920
When he was born circa 1341 BC, his personal
name was actually Tutankhaten, meaning “the

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.470
living image of Aten.”

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:21.980
This was because of his father, Akhenaten
or Amenhotep IV, who was one of the most controversial

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:26.760
pharaohs in history and someone you will likely
see on this channel in the future.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:31.120
The religion of ancient Egypt is still pretty
well-known to this day as we’ve all heard

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:37.439
of gods like Horus, and Anubis, and Osiris,
and, most important of all, the Sun God Amun-Ra.

00:03:37.439 --> 00:03:43.259
Well, Akhenaten decided to do away with all
of that and focus worship on a single deity

00:03:43.259 --> 00:03:45.120
- Aten the sun disk.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:49.819
The pharaoh even had a new city built dedicated
to the god which was intended to function

00:03:49.819 --> 00:03:51.450
as the new capital of his empire.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:54.019
He called it Akhetaten, modern day Amarna.

00:03:54.019 --> 00:03:58.280
Suffice to say that the people did not take
too kindly to this religious revolution.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:04.139
After Akhenaten died, they quickly relocated
the capital back to Thebes and went back to

00:04:04.139 --> 00:04:05.190
their old religion.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:10.139
They even submitted Akhenaten to damnatio
memoriae, the practice where they try to completely

00:04:10.139 --> 00:04:13.769
wipe him from history by erasing his name
from all inscriptions.

00:04:13.769 --> 00:04:18.130
Well, we are talking about him right now so,
clearly, they did not do a very good job,

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:23.280
but this is why Tutankhamun originally had
the name Tutankhaten and why he changed it

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.280
afterwards.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:28.530
As far as Tut’s mother goes, she is a bit
more of a mystery since surviving inscriptions

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.370
do not make her identity clear.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:35.300
Some egyptologists argue that his mother was
Nefertiti herself, the famous Egyptian queen

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:40.170
who was Akhenaten’s main wife, or Great
Royal Wife, as she was called.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:45.070
Others are convinced that his mother was an
unnamed mummy discovered over a century ago,

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:47.360
referred to simply as the Younger Lady.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:51.390
Modern DNA tests support this assertion, but
some experts are still not convinced.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:56.040
Some of them argue that the tests are inconclusive
due to decayed samples while others opine

00:04:56.040 --> 00:05:01.380
that the mummy is, in fact, Nefertiti, as
her remains have never been found.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:07.510
The Reign of King Tut

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:11.290
Tutankhamun’s ascension to the throne is
somewhat murky because, as we said, later

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:15.180
pharaohs tried to make it look like that part
of their history never happened.

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:20.380
To the best of our knowledge, Akhenaten reigned
for 17 years and was followed by two short

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:23.070
reigns before Tutankhamun took the throne.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:29.130
Those reigns belonged to Smenkhkare, a pharaoh
about whom we know almost nothing, and Neferneferuaten,

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:35.280
a female pharaoh who was, most likely, Nefertiti,
or one of Akhenaten’s daughters.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:40.830
One or both of them may have reigned as co-regents
with Akhenaten prior to his death.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:44.540
Around 1334 BC, Tutankhamun assumed power.

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:48.860
He was still just a young boy, only eight
or nine years old, so his decisions were heavily

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.930
influenced by his advisors.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:56.270
Particularly, one advisor named Ay who served
at the king’s court since the time of Akhenaten.

00:05:56.270 --> 00:06:00.100
It is believed he was the main power hiding
in the shadows who actually made the decisions

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:05.200
during Tut’s reign and, indeed, after the
young king died, Ay became the new pharaoh.

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:09.680
He only lasted for a few years before he was
succeeded by another one of Tut’s officials,

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:14.360
Horemheb, who ended up serving as the last
pharaoh of the 18th dynasty.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:17.540
Tutankhamun’s 10-year reign as ruler of
Egypt was unremarkable.

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:21.361
The country was still in chaos due to his
father’s religious revolution and the young

00:06:21.361 --> 00:06:27.040
pharaoh, undoubtedly guided by his advisors,
renounced his father’s ideas and began restoring

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:30.490
things to how they were before the Amarna
period.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:35.750
This mostly involved rebuilding temples, monuments,
and stelae which were either destroyed or

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:41.590
defaced during the time of Akhenaten; abandoning
the city of Akhetaten and moving the capital

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:47.480
back to Thebes, and changing his name from
Tut-ankh-aten to Tut-ankh-amun to show the

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:50.130
pharaoh’s devotion to the once-mighty god.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:54.440
Tut married his half-sister, Ankhesenamun,
and together they had two daughters who both

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:55.560
died in infancy.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:59.820
Some scholars believe that the queen went
on to marry Ay after Tutankhamun’s death,

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:02.360
but there isn’t conclusive evidence to support
this.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:07.310
Perhaps the most noteworthy event that happened
during that time came courtesy not of King

00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:09.180
Tut, but his wife.

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:13.550
After the young pharaoh’s death, Ankhesenamun
may have wrote a letter to the King of the

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:21.870
Hittites, Suppiluliuma I, asking for one of
his sons in marriage.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:26.720
The Hittites had long been a thorn in Egypt’s
side and, taking advantage of the chaos during

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:30.140
the reign of Akhenaten, they grew to be just
as powerful.

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:33.450
It would have been the first time that the
son of a foreign king would have ruled over

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:36.810
Egypt and, obviously, Suppiluliuma was over
the moon with this idea.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:41.270
He sent his son, Prince Zannanza, to marry
Ankhesenamun, but he died somewhere on the

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:42.270
way.

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:45.260
The exact circumstances of his death are not
known, although many speculate that he was

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:49.820
assassinated on the orders of Ay or Horemheb
(or both).

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:53.670
As for Tutankhamun, like we said, his reign
was nothing to write home about.

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:57.320
The boy king would surely have been relegated
to a footnote in the history books were it

00:07:57.320 --> 00:08:21.460
not for the events that occurred thousands
of years after his death in 1325 BC.

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:56.980
Death Is

00:08:56.980 --> 00:09:08.110
Only the Beginning

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:14.820
We now leave ancient Egypt and travel over
3,000 years into the future.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:19.360
We are in the same region, which is now known
as the Valley of the Kings because it had

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:23.980
been used as a burial site for pharaohs and
other important ancient officials for almost

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:24.980
500 years.

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:29.980
It had been excavated by archaeologists since
the early 1800s and, at the start of the 20th

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:34.440
century, there was a belief that everything
there was to be found had already been found.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:38.800
The man in charge of the excavations, American
explorer Theodore Davis, famously ended a

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:45.040
paper published in 1912 with the words “I
fear that the Valley of the Kings is now exhausted.”

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:50.540
Davis died in 1915 and the rights to excavate
the valley were bought by an English aristocrat

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:53.330
named George Herbert, the 5th Earl of Carnarvon.

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:57.750
He had in his employ an archaeologist named
Howard Carter who had been digging for him

00:09:57.750 --> 00:10:01.310
since 1907, but without any tremendous success.

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:05.630
Carter relocated to the Valley of the Kings
and resumed his work for Lord Carnarvon but,

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:08.920
again, many years went by without any significant
discoveries.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:14.690
In 1922, Carnarvon started to feel like Davis
may have been right all along and there truly

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:16.880
wasn’t anything left in the Valley of the
Kings.

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:21.840
He told Carter that he would only fund one
more season of digging before he abandoned

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:22.840
the valley for good.

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:27.330
Carter’s time was running out but, in November
of that year, he made the discovery of the

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:28.330
century.

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:32.840
According to his own journal, the serendipitous
moment occurred by accident on November 4th

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:35.350
when his water boy stumbled over a stone.

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:39.660
Upon closer inspection, that stone turned
out to be the top of a set of stairs buried

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:41.010
in the sand.

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:45.730
Understandably excited, Carter excavated the
spot and found that the stairs led to a burial

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:48.550
site of great significance based on the royal
seals.

00:10:48.550 --> 00:10:53.110
He wrote to Lord Carnarvon and waited for
the arrival of his benefactor before going

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:54.110
inside.

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:58.070
On November 26, Carter, Carnarvon and his
daughter, Evelyn Herbert, became the first

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:02.440
people to enter the tomb of Tutankhamun in
over 3,000 years.

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:06.990
Almost immediately, the archaeologist realized
the magnitude of the find as he saw “everywhere

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:11.740
the glint of gold” - statues, cups, beds,
and even a throne filled an antechamber which

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:13.810
led to another room with a sealed doorway.

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:18.170
At this point, it wasn’t clear yet what
Carter had found - was this simply a treasure

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:22.560
cache or was there an actual burial chamber
waiting for them behind that doorway?

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:24.390
They had to wait a bit to get their answer.

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:29.550
It wasn’t until February 1923 that Carter
was finally able to enter the closed chamber

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:33.650
and glimpse, for the first time, the sarcophagus
of Tutankhamun.

00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:38.160
Afterwards, Carter and his team spent the
next decade cataloguing, preserving and removing

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:42.040
over 5,000 objects that were sitting in that
tomb.

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:47.240
Inside the Tomb

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:52.880
The tomb of Tutankhamun which was designated
KV62 consisted of four rooms, a corridor,

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:54.020
and a staircase.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:57.980
Contrary to what is commonly believed, the
burial site was not completely pristine.

00:11:57.980 --> 00:12:01.750
It had actually been targeted by thieves in
the past, it’s just that the looting happened

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:06.340
soon after Tut’s burial and Egyptian officials
had time to fix the problem.

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:09.530
Some of the doors showed signs of repairs
and being sealed more than once.

00:12:09.530 --> 00:12:11.830
It appears that the tomb was robbed twice.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:14.880
First time, the thief or thieves didn’t
get away with much, but they did steal things

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:19.600
like oils and cosmetics which were highly
prized in ancient Egyptian society.

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:23.520
Such items would not have lasted long so,
obviously, the theft occurred soon after the

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:25.330
objects were placed inside the tomb.

00:12:25.330 --> 00:12:29.990
The second occasion was more complex and organized
and involved digging a tunnel inside the burial

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:32.210
chamber and accessing the treasury.

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:36.540
That room was filled with jewelry and, while
thieves stole a lot of it, the scene suggested

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:40.730
that they had been caught in the act and had
to make a hasty getaway which was why they

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:42.430
left so much stuff behind.

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:47.280
Even with these acts of vandalism, KV62 was
still the most complete pharaoh’s tomb ever

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.280
discovered.

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:51.730
Then, of course, there was the burial chamber,
the main event, as it were, which contained

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:53.350
the mummy of the boy king.

00:12:53.350 --> 00:12:57.399
This was the only room which had decorations
on the walls which depicted the pharaoh and

00:12:57.399 --> 00:13:00.830
multiple deities taking part in various ceremonies.

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:04.700
The bulk of the room was taken up by four
gilded shrines made out of wood.

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:09.420
The shrines were each smaller than the last
and were placed inside each other like Russian

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:13.740
nesting dolls and, inside the smallest shrine,
there was the sarcophagus.

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:18.390
Inside the sarcophagus we had a similar situation
as the mummy was placed inside three coffins.

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:22.130
The outer two were made of gilded wood like
the shrines, but it was the innermost coffin

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:28.470
which immediately attracted attention as it
was made of over 240 lbs of pure gold.

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:33.250
Inside the coffin was the pharaoh’s mummy,
of course, wearing a gold funerary mask adorned

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:37.610
with precious jewels which has probably become
the most famous artifact from ancient Egypt.

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:42.080
As egyptologists studied this treasure trove
of artifacts, they couldn’t help but notice

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:46.370
that this tomb may have never been intended
for Tutankhamun at all.

00:13:46.370 --> 00:13:50.790
Some items showed signs that they previously
contained different names which had been erased

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:53.560
and “Tutankhamun” written on top of them.

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:57.370
This alone could have been explained simply
by officials wanting to remove the pharaoh’s

00:13:57.370 --> 00:13:58.940
original name, Tutankhaten.

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:02.860
However, there were plenty of other curious
features which suggested that the tomb was

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:04.550
originally built for an older man.

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:09.180
The most common theory is that it was intended
for Smenkhkare, the mysterious pharaoh that

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:11.110
ruled for a little bit before King Tut.

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:15.660
For decades, scholars have argued over the
possibility of there being more chambers hidden

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:17.490
inside KV62.

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:21.550
One of them could even contain the elusive
resting place of Nefertiti.

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:26.279
But this argument seemed destined to remain
unsettled since, for obvious reasons, nobody

00:14:26.279 --> 00:14:30.510
was allowed to start smashing up the burial
chamber in search of undiscovered rooms.

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:36.260
However, modern technology provided us with
an unintrusive solution to the problem - ground-penetrating

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:37.580
radar scans.

00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:39.540
This technique was not without controversy.

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:44.920
The first scans took place in 2015 and detected
the presence of open spaces which backed up

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:47.960
the idea that there was more to find in Tut’s
tomb.

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:50.550
However, a subsequent test failed to replicate
these results.

00:14:50.550 --> 00:14:55.640
A third and final scan was performed in 2018
by three different companies which negated

00:14:55.640 --> 00:14:58.950
the initial findings and detected nothing
but solid rock.

00:14:58.950 --> 00:15:04.200
The Egyptian Ministry of Antiquities has accepted
these results and there are no plans to search

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:05.200
for more chambers in the near future.

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:09.720
As far as the items inside the tomb are concerned,
we are obviously not going to talk about all

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:12.480
of them since there are over 5,000 of them.

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:16.740
We already mentioned the most important ones,
but there are a few more curious objects that

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:17.810
merit inclusion.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:21.770
For example, the tomb contained a pair of
trumpets, one silver and the other either

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:26.290
bronze or copper, which may be the oldest
still-functional trumpets in the world.

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:31.600
These ancient instruments were actually played
once in 1939, on an international BBC broadcast

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:35.060
which was heard by approximately 150 million
people.

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:38.320
There is one final item to mention which is
out of this world...literally.

00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:41.950
It is a dagger whose blade was made out of
iron meteorite.

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:47.310
Its exact origins are unclear as the quality
metalwork is uncharacteristic of Egypt in

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:52.750
Tut’s time so either ancient Egyptians were
far more skilled iron craftsmen than we previously

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:55.610
thought or the dagger was a gift from another
place.

00:15:55.610 --> 00:16:00.269
Its extraterrestrial credentials were confirmed
with the help of a spectrometer which detected

00:16:00.269 --> 00:16:06.010
high levels of nickel and cobalt, indicative
of meteoritic iron.

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:10.500
The Mummy

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:14.970
Studying all the artifacts inside the tomb
was all well &amp; good, but what about the mummy?

00:16:14.970 --> 00:16:18.460
It won’t surprise you to learn that the
body of Tutankhamun has been examined and

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:19.540
discussed extensively.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:25.110
It probably also won’t surprise you to discover
that the young, inbred king wasn’t exactly

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:26.510
the peak of good health.

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:31.060
In fact, he was frail, disabled, suffered
from one or more genetic abnormalities, and

00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:33.310
probably needed a cane to walk around.

00:16:33.310 --> 00:16:37.220
Before we get into any specifics, we should
mention that Tutankhamun’s health is the

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:41.480
subject of multiple studies and many of them
contradict or disagree with each other so

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:46.519
there isn’t universal acceptance regarding
the pharaoh’s health problems and they also

00:16:46.519 --> 00:16:48.649
include a fair bit of speculation.

00:16:48.649 --> 00:16:50.340
Let’s start with the minor stuff.

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:54.510
Tut had several features which were believed
to be genetic traits of his bloodline.

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:59.769
They included a small cleft palate, an overbite,
and larger-than-normal center incisors.

00:16:59.769 --> 00:17:04.750
He also had an unusually elongated skull shape
which, again, was thought to be an abnormality

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:06.170
that ran in the family.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:09.740
Tut had trouble walking and, although it was
initially believed this was due to a stress

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:14.309
fracture caused by an accident, recent research
indicates that he was actually born with a

00:17:14.309 --> 00:17:15.660
severe club foot.

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:19.919
His condition may have gotten even worse as
the years went by as he may have also suffered

00:17:19.919 --> 00:17:23.329
from a degenerative bone condition called
Kohler disease.

00:17:23.329 --> 00:17:27.520
His spine was curved and showed fusion in
the upper vertebrae which some believed could

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:32.101
have been a sign of Marfan’s syndrome, although
this idea was later dismissed by the most

00:17:32.101 --> 00:17:33.330
recent tests.

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:37.050
The malformation on his leg would have been
so extreme that the pharaoh would not have

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:38.600
been able to walk without a cane.

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:42.830
As proof of this, scholars point to the fact
that over 100 walking canes were buried with

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:44.250
the young king in his tomb.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:48.850
There is a reason why not everyone is onboard
with this idea and it is because it cancels

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:52.700
out one of the main theories regarding Tutankhamun’s
death.

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:57.200
Some egyptologists are of the firm opinion
that the boy king died from injuries suffered

00:17:57.200 --> 00:17:58.410
in a chariot crash.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:03.170
However, if his foot was as bad as this new
study indicates, then it would have been impossible

00:18:03.170 --> 00:18:04.930
for him to ride in a chariot.

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:08.740
This brings us neatly to our next point - what
killed Tutankhamun?

00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:13.049
There is no mention of his cause of death
in ancient records and examining his remains

00:18:13.049 --> 00:18:14.700
didn’t reveal an obvious answer.

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:19.059
For decades, it was believed that Tut’s
death came as the result of foul play.

00:18:19.059 --> 00:18:23.590
X-ray scans performed in the 1960s showed
that the young pharaoh had bone fragments

00:18:23.590 --> 00:18:26.750
inside his skull, indicative of a blow to
the head.

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:30.980
However, newer tests revealed that the bits
of bone ended up there in modern times, when

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:33.090
the mummy was removed from its coffin.

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:36.130
There were no other signs to suggest a fatal
head blow.

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:40.200
Then there is the aforementioned “chariot
crash theory” which asserts that Tutankhamun

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:45.130
died either due to direct injuries sustained
in a chariot crash or from an infection that

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:46.340
came as a result of it.

00:18:46.340 --> 00:18:50.630
Adherents of this idea point to damage done
to the young king’s ribs and chest which

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:55.030
could be indicative of crushing injuries,
plus images in his tomb that depict the pharaoh

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:56.710
riding a chariot in battle.

00:18:56.710 --> 00:19:01.020
Again, opponents of this theory believe these
injuries were caused recently while handling

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:02.020
the mummy.

00:19:02.020 --> 00:19:06.070
The most up-to-date research actually suggests
that Tut died from malaria.

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:10.350
Tests performed a decade ago found traces
of the infection in four mummies, including

00:19:10.350 --> 00:19:11.350
Tutankhamun.

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:15.240
This, compounded with all the other health
problems that lowered his immune system, could

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:18.670
be the culprit that cut the pharaoh’s reign
short.

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:23.280
There is no universally-accepted solution,
but this is, at the moment, the most prevalent

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:24.280
theory.

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:28.640
The obsession with death surrounding Tutankhamun
hasn’t really been restricted to his own

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:29.640
demise.

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:33.450
After all, many other people died after the
tomb was opened because they dared to disturb

00:19:33.450 --> 00:19:34.670
the sleep of the pharaoh.

00:19:34.670 --> 00:19:35.670
Didn’t they?

00:19:35.670 --> 00:19:39.400
Yes, we’ve all heard about the notorious
curse of the pharaohs.

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:43.700
It has been mentioned since the 19th century,
but it was the discovery of Tut’s tomb that

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:47.640
made it infinitely more popular and helped
it reach the public consciousness.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:52.590
Although, curiously, there is no actual curse
inscribed anywhere inside KV62.

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:53.920
It was a fabrication of the newspapers.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:54.920
This was more of an Old Kingdom practice,
while Tut’s 18th dynasty ruled firmly during

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:55.920
the New Kingdom.

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.710
There is one suspicious death surrounding
the discovery of the tomb, one single death

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:01.730
that set off the mania of the “mummy’s
curse.”.

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:05.450
Lord Carnarvon, the man who funded Carter’s
digging, died a few months after entering

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:06.450
the tomb.

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:11.540
He succumbed to blood poisoning and the newspapers
immediately started touting the “curse of

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:12.540
the pharaohs.”

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:17.170
Since then, anything bad or remotely suspicious
that happened to one of the dozens of people

00:20:17.170 --> 00:20:20.330
involved with the mummy was ascribed to the
curse.

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:23.880
However, the British Medical Journal actually
did a scientific study and found that the

00:20:23.880 --> 00:20:27.990
life expectancy rate for those people wasn’t
higher or lower than the average.

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:32.400
It was just that the abnormal cases received
much more media attention.

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:37.340
The study also debunked another notion which
said that there was a more direct way in which

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:43.150
the tomb caused the demise of Carnarvon and
others - ancient mold spores which they inhaled

00:20:43.150 --> 00:20:46.150
and caused damage to their respiratory systems.

00:20:46.150 --> 00:20:49.140
This didn’t happen, either, and, if it did,
it would have killed them a lot sooner, not

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:50.700
in months or years.

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:59.380
So you can rest assured that, should you ever
disturb the pharaoh’s slumber, you will

00:20:59.380 --> 00:21:14.950
not be cursed...probably.

